      "lineNbr": 41,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-02T16:28:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The static lib doesn\u0027t compile against hidden APIs, and therefore TestableNetworkCallback can\u0027t compile against LocalNetworkInfo until it\u0027s API.\n\nIt seems dangerous to have the static lib compile against hidden API, as it would be very easy to use a static method that tries to access a hidden API in production code.\n\nOne solution would be to fragment our static lib even more than it already is between the parts that can only be used in tests and can link against hidden symbols, and the parts that can\u0027t. This would complexify substantially the already really complex build files.",
      "parentUuid": "91236a8c_8b4dd2c5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 41,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 41,
        "endChar": 53
      },
      "revId": "ea311a7c4e0fab259da3ee76eebd8dd59c999147",
